\name{cellucid_my_datasets_forget}
\alias{cellucid_my_datasets_forget}
\title{Forget a dataset of My datasets}
\usage{
cellucid_my_datasets_forget(viewer, name, saved_states = FALSE)
}
\arguments{
\item{viewer}{A viewer \code{\link{cellucid_view}()} or \code{\link{cellucid_serve}()} returned.}
\item{name}{Its name in My datasets (datasets_list). Text (at least 1 character). Required.}
\item{saved_states}{Also delete its saved states (histories kept in this browser). \code{TRUE} or \code{FALSE}. Default \code{FALSE}, the viewer's own.}
}
\value{
A \code{cellucid_action_request}, at once and invisibly: the action is sent now, or when the viewer's channel opens.
\code{\link{cellucid_action_result}(request)} returns its outcome: a list of \code{handles} (Handles of files of this computer forgotten with it), \code{name} (The dataset forgotten), \code{saved_states} (Its saved states deleted).
}
\description{
Remove one dataset from My datasets, as its Forget in My datasets \ifelse{latex}{<U+203A>}{›} All\ldots does: the entry and, for a file or folder of this computer, the browser's handle of it; its saved states only when asked. The dataset itself is not touched, and nothing brings the entry back but opening it again.
}
\details{
The viewer's action \code{my-datasets.forget} (Datasets). It acts outside the viewer's state and history (a file the person receives in the browser, a publication, or what the browser keeps for later visits), which Undo does not take back: it makes no step of the history.

When an agent (Claude, ChatGPT) runs it, the viewer asks the person first (deletes-saved); from R it is not asked.
}
\seealso{
\code{\link{cellucid_act}()} sends any action by its type, and \code{\link{cellucid_action_result}()}
collects its answer.
}
\examples{
if (interactive() && requireNamespace("SeuratObject", quietly = TRUE)) {
  data("pbmc_small", package = "SeuratObject")
  viewer <- cellucid_view(SeuratObject::UpdateSeuratObject(pbmc_small))
  request <- cellucid_my_datasets_forget(viewer, name = "Pancreatic endocrinogenesis (scVelo)")
  print(request)
  # cellucid_action_result(request) waits for its outcome.
  cellucid_stop(viewer)
}
}
